      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": "three-hybrid",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Finally, you can mix and match the three list types within a single hybrid list. The AsciiDoc syntax tries hard to infer the relationships between the items that are most intuitive to us humans."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s a list that mixes description, ordered, and unordered lists. Notice how the term delimiter is changed from "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "::"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ":::"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to create a nested description list."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Operating Systems::\n  Linux:::\n    . Fedora\n      * Desktop\n    . Ubuntu\n      * Desktop\n      * Server\n  BSD:::\n    . FreeBSD\n    . NetBSD\n\nCloud Providers::\n  PaaS:::\n    . OpenShift\n    . CloudBees\n  IaaS:::\n    . Amazon EC2\n    . Rackspace"
